---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Naturo Group collects, uses and protects your personal information under the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles."
  updated="27 April 2026"
>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} ("Naturo Group", "we", "our", "us") is committed to protecting your
    privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, hold, use and disclose personal
    information in accordance with the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth) and the Australian
    Privacy Principles (APPs).
  </p>

  <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
  <p>We may collect the following personal information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Identity and contact details: name, phone number, email address, and service address.</li>
    <li>Service details: home size, number of bedrooms / bathrooms, requested services, scheduling preferences and access instructions.</li>
    <li>Eligibility information for funded programs (e.g. NDIS, DVA, Aged Care, Insurance) where you ask us to act for you.</li>
    <li>Payment and billing information processed by our payment provider (we do not store full card numbers).</li>
    <li>Website usage data such as IP address, device type, browser, pages visited, referring URL, and marketing campaign parameters (UTM, gclid, fbclid).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we collect it</h2>
  <p>
    We collect personal information directly from you when you request a quote, book a
    service, contact us by phone or email, apply for employment, or interact with our website.
    We may also receive information from third parties such as plan managers, support
    coordinators, insurers, case managers or referrers, where you have asked them to share
    your details with us.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>We use personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide quotes, bookings and the cleaning services you request.</li>
    <li>Communicate with you about your booking, including reminders and follow-ups.</li>
    <li>Invoice your plan manager, insurer or case manager where applicable.</li>
    <li>Improve our services, website and customer experience.</li>
    <li>Send marketing communications, where you have given consent and have not opted out.</li>
    <li>Comply with our legal, insurance and regulatory obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We may share your personal information with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Our trained, police-checked cleaning team members assigned to your job.</li>
    <li>Service providers who help us run our business (form intake, email, SMS, calendar, payments, hosting, analytics).</li>
    <li>Your plan manager, insurer, case manager or referrer where you have asked us to deal with them on your behalf.</li>
    <li>Law enforcement, regulators or courts where required by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information.</p>

  <h2>5. Overseas disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Some of our service providers (for example our website hosting, form intake and email
    providers) may store data on servers located outside Australia, including in the United
    States and the European Union. We take reasonable steps to ensure these providers handle
    your information consistently with the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We retain personal information only for as long as we need it for the purposes described
    above, or as required by law (for example, taxation and insurance record-keeping
    requirements). Quote enquiries that do not become bookings are typically retained for up
    to 24 months for follow-up and service improvement, then de-identified or deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable technical and organisational steps to protect personal information
    from misuse, interference, loss, unauthorised access, modification or disclosure. No
    system is completely secure; if we become aware of a notifiable data breach we will
    comply with our obligations under Part IIIC of the Privacy Act.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Request access to the personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Ask us to correct information that is inaccurate, out of date or incomplete.</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent for marketing communications at any time.</li>
    <li>Make a complaint about how we have handled your personal information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details below. We will respond
    within a reasonable period (usually 30 days). If you are not satisfied with our response,
    you may complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) at
    <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener" target="_blank">oaic.gov.au</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Cookies & tracking</h2>
  <p>
    We use cookies, browser storage and similar technologies. See our
    <a href="/cookies-data-policy">Cookies & Data Policy</a> for details
    and how to control them.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top
    of this page reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be highlighted on
    our website.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName}<br />
    {site.abn}<br />
    Email: <a href={site.emailHref}>{site.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
  </p>
</LegalPage>
